// 5/3/1 Core Stability, barebones: the same four days (press, deadlift,
// bench, squat) and four weeks, the last a deload, cut to three parts. Each
// day runs: the two-movement core-stability pair, the Leg dynamic stretch
// block, then the main lift. No accessories, foam rolling or static stretching.
//
// The 1RM lines below are TRAINING MAXES, which is what Wendler's
// percentages are taken from. Edit them before generating; add 5lb (upper) /
// 10lb (lower) each cycle. The + set is as many good reps as you have.
//
// Core pairs (Big 3 variations): press - side plank leg lift, 6-position
// carry; deadlift - around the worlds, renegade rows; bench - Milco bench
// press, ab-wheel rollout; squat - cable chops and lifts, stir the pot.
// Overhead Press 1RM: 120lb
// Deadlift 1RM: 290lb
// Flat Barbell Bench Press 1RM: 225lb
// Barbell Squat 1RM: 245lb

